**Addendum (owner directive, live-test follow-up): `3bc3d30d35` — unanswered inbound agent mail is never a compaction candidate.

**Trigger.** A live clip from a DAP multi-agent session: a peer's mail delivered into a busy agent, the autonomous chain then paused on its budget with one message queued — while earlier delivered-but-unanswered mail was foldable by every mechanical tier. The prompt-level belt (`## Open User Requests`, #81 v2) is judgment-only (AC9: the summarizer LLM judges openness), and the ledger's `kind=='user'` exempt tag only binds the JUDGE — the relief's keep-N hide, the checkpoint foldable range, and the local trim valve all folded delivered mail like noise. The channel delivery shape (`from <id> in #<channel>:`) additionally escapes the DM-only `_agentMailPattern` in `isSyntheticUserText`.

**The belt (`compaction/inbound_mail.dart`).** One record- and message-level definition consumed by all tiers:
- `isAgentMailText` (user_text.dart): DM shape, channel shape, reply anchor;
- a mail record with no later reply never enters the engine's foldable range, never passes `validateHidePicks` (pinned), never joins the relief's keep-N veto (passes 1/2), and the trim valve CARRIES it across the cut like the pinned newest user turn;
- reply evidence is deliberately conservative: an `agent_message` tool call or pure prose closes the mail; ordinary tool-call carriers are the agent working, not answering (the naive any-assistant rule made the invariant dead code in agentic sessions — caught by the tests before it shipped);
- answered mail folds like any other data (protection stays bounded).

**Scope decision.** Channel mail intentionally stays OUT of `isSyntheticUserText` — flipping it changes newest-real-user-turn semantics far beyond this belt (obligations ledger, checkpoint auto-close, gh-241 pin tests). The unanswered-mail invariant is the targeted fix.

**Validation.** 16 new tests (`inbound_mail_test.dart`): text shapes, record/message matrices, validateHidePicks pins incl. the judge-exempt regression guard, valve carry/drop, relief end-to-end (fixture geometry pinned: transcript > relief target, newest result inside the valve's keep budget, so the carried path actually runs). Full `test/compaction/` + `auto_compactor`: 955 green; analyze clean.

Also captured in this thread: live validation runs of the PR's compaction stack on a copy of a real 544 KB DAP session — manual `/compact` (judge call to glm-5.3-flash, honest empty-range hand-over) and a fully AUTO `structured·hand-over` pass at cap 34000 (82 records hidden, 29848→18642 tokens, −38%, durable checkpoint with identities/agreements/verbatim errors preserved).
